# Hypermedia update contract (cursor-packs)

When adding or changing Datastar `patch-elements`, htmx swaps, templ SSE morphs, or `data-on:click` actions that must refresh server-owned UI:

- Load skill `hypermedia-update-contract`.

Two patch contracts:

- **Command / board:** the same view function as the initial GET, fat-morphed onto one workspace root.
- **Progress / activity:** plan and activity only. MUST NOT reuse the command fragment when it includes proposal or editor chrome.

`data-ignore-morph` and client signals do not update approval, pending review, or whether run controls are enabled. Those come from the post-commit read model inside the command patch.
